wer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6cea381-d89c-5a7b-a546-90c344bcd752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413979} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8825eea-6236-5c45-a6bf-fa0d2e334802" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da6ab59f-cfd7-5d6f-94dd-f3fddb0a05c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-253391" :question/problem "Let ${J}_{n}(\\lambda )$ denote an $n\\times n$ Jordan block with $\\lambda $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({J}_{3}(2))=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=\\begin{bmatrix}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ $n=3,$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\nSince $n=3,$ we need to compute the first $3-1=2$ derivative of $f:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{3}(2)) & =\\begin{bmatrix}f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) & \\frac{1}{2!}{f}^{″}(2) \\\\ 0 & f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡2 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d5712b5-5792-554d-8f40-73fe534ecc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|A|\\ne |B|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414255} {:answer/id #uuid "81741bfd-a764-5fc4-911b-02c9e77b0036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81741bfd-a764-5fc4-911b-02c9e77b0036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|A|=|B|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414297} :answer-field/id #uuid "1660089b-aae2-502e-8705-8096b17a3d97" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0299bb8a-9915-5ed0-b427-9ea16c7bfd20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414229} {:answer/id #uuid "6a7d1b24-9b0d-5df5-a3dd-b9407461dedd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "surjective" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414280} {:answer/id #uuid "d3694270-c310-557a-9b25-b3086212444f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "increasing" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a7d1b24-9b0d-5df5-a3dd-b9407461dedd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "surjective" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414280} :answer-field/id #uuid "640e6638-9a90-5297-900d-9fa809a0cc7b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414384} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09b85ac8-c2b1-53d7-a521-87ffe25b001f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "injective" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414232} {:answer/id #uuid "127b45c4-962f-5a5c-95b9-c12750fcc897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414236} {:answer/id #uuid "f2c2f1fb-2b60-5dfc-8ea1-19e9e9ac54a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09b85ac8-c2b1-53d7-a521-87ffe25b001f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "injective" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414232} :answer-field/id #uuid "8285bc18-0c23-50ae-b5c6-2fd192928624" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31bc4e24-a07b-5170-8926-cd699cf0f86a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{18}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414256} {:answer/id #uuid "4c242cb5-3b92-57ed-ab90-2cdee34992fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{(\\frac{16}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414266} {:answer/id #uuid "7424f06b-159b-5c56-8bb1-e4165486d93e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cdot {6}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414287} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab1a084-e3fa-517d-98bf-385373080007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414293} {:answer/id #uuid "eafe5b8c-fdac-5f2f-8c20-f4eb3dda569f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\cdot {3}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ab1a084-e3fa-517d-98bf-385373080007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414293} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8924976-ac1d-5805-ab82-ea80f8fb3b09" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a1686501-a304-5a7a-bf6f-4c7790651929" :question/math-academy-id "q-216550" :question/problem "$$\nA=N,\\,B=\\{18,\\,12,\\,8,\\,\\frac{16}{3},\\,…\\}\n$$\n\nComplete the following reasoning about the sets $A$ and $B$ (shown above):\n\nSince the function $f:A\\to B,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf:n\\to {{field-1}}\n$$\n\nis both {{field-2}} and {{field-3}}, we have that {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Two sets $A$ and $B$ have the *same cardinality* if there exists a bijection between $A$ and $B.$\n\nNotice that the elements of $B$ form an (infinite) geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=\\frac{2}{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{12} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $n$th term of our geometric sequence, denoted ${a}_{n},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =18{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express $B$ in set-builder notation as \n\n$$\nB=\\{18{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}\\,|\\,\\,n\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, consider the function $f:A\\to B$ that maps the underlying sets as follows: \n\n| $A$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $⋯$ | $n$ | $⋯$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $B$ | $18$ | $12$ | $8$ | $\\frac{16}{3}$ | $⋯$ | $18{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}$ | $⋯$ |\n\nIn general, for each $n\\in A,$ we have $f(n)=18{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{n-1}\\in B.$\n\nNotice that $f$ is described in such a way that it is bijective. Indeed, it's\n\n- injective since $f(n)\\ne f(m)$ whenever $n\\ne m,$ and\n\n- surjective since each element in $B$ (the second row) has a pre-image in $A$ (the first row).\n\nTherefore, $|A|=|B|,$ i.e., the sets have the same cardinality."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab0679db-895a-5a46-9a05-9b44fb8f1e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "surjective" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414315} {:answer/id #uuid "b51f41ec-ff36-5e1c-ac65-318bd0b22be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414322} {:answer/id #uuid "d98081a8-2046-5b75-ac9e-78b3fc9d7683" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "increasing" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab0679db-895a-5a46-9a05-9b44fb8f1e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "surjective" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414315} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ecdd120-3ad6-57f9-b83b-764594ebf2c7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23945915-4c04-59b5-9258-20a54b3f1b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiable" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414247} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee305bc-7787-5d82-a06a-107208f20ed1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "positive" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414271}